<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Imperial-Royal Landwehr</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1869–1918</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as k.k. Landwehr</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Imperial-Royal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landwehr">Landwehr</a> was the territorial army of the Austrian half of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a>, created in 1869 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-compromise-of-1867">Compromise of 1867</a> alongside the joint <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imperial-and-royal-army">Imperial and Royal Army</a> and the Hungarian Honvéd. At first a reserve force, it became a full front-line army before 1914 and fought throughout the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/imperial-royal-landwehr.jpg" alt="Imperial-Royal Landwehr" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Felipe Fidelis Tobias · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Regimental_Flag_of_the_Imperial-Royal_Landwehr,_Cerimonial_Flag_of_the_Gardebataillon_and_Standard_of_the_Common_Army_(Obverse).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
